@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+type: fix
+issue: 8822
+title: "On a server with full-text indexing disabled, expanding a ValueSet included every code its `compose.include`
+  listed, even codes the CodeSystem does not have. Once the ValueSet was pre-expanded, `ValueSet/$validate-code`
+  accepted those codes and `:in` searches matched resources that use them. These codes are now left out of the
+  expansion, as they already were with full-text indexing enabled. This includes a CodeSystem with
+  `content` `not-present`: a ValueSet listing codes from it now expands to no codes instead of every listed code.
+  Expansions stored before the upgrade keep these codes until the ValueSet is expanded again, for example after
+  calling `$invalidate-expansion` on it."
